---

<ProjectPageLayout
  title="RBH-1 Validation & Reanalysis"
  tagline="Independent analysis of the hypervelocity SMBH bow shock candidate"
  status="Active"
  heroImage="/images/projects/rbh1-validation.jpg"
  githubUrl="https://github.com/radioastronomyio/rbh1-validation-reanalysis"
  description="Independent validation and reanalysis of the RBH-1 hypervelocity supermassive black hole candidate using Bayesian inference and GPU-accelerated computing."
>
  <section>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Overview</h2>
    <p class="text-brand-gray dark:text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">Independent validation and reanalysis of the RBH-1 hypervelocity supermassive black hole candidate (van Dokkum et al. 2025) using Bayesian inference and GPU-accelerated computing.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Research Context</h2>
    <p class="text-brand-gray dark:text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">RBH-1 was proposed as a runaway supermassive black hole ejected from its host galaxy, with a luminous trail interpreted as a bow shock. This project provides independent reanalysis to test the hypothesis against alternative explanations.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Approach</h2>
    <ul class="space-y-2 text-brand-gray dark:text-gray-400">
      <li>Analysis-Ready Dataset construction from HST/JWST observations</li>
      <li>Bayesian model comparison (bow shock vs. edge-on galaxy)</li>
      <li>GPU-accelerated MCMC sampling</li>
      <li>Transparent methodology with full reproducibility</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</ProjectPageLayout>
